WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.060
Sana-chan...

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:07.970
Sana...

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:10.390
Sana...

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.060
Sana-chan!

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:38.640
Aoi-chan?

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:45.840
Are you okay?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.430
Ah, yeah.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.190
I'm sorry.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:01.060
It's really just like you to nearly fall when there's nothing there.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:03.690
Really?

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.570
I wasn't actually praising you though.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.730
Really?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>Aoi-chan sure hasn't changed one bit.</i>

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.040
<i>Even though some parts of her have really changed.</i>

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.190
Sana-chan! I'm talking to you, Sana-chan!

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:23.530
What is it?

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.630
What's wrong? You just spaced-out.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.010
Oh, my.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.640
Hey, be careful not to walk while spaced-out!

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:35.440
Ow, that hurts!

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.050
<i>I think you're the one who needs to be careful...</i>

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:47.200
Hey!

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.040
Shuu?

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.150
Morning, Sana.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.920
Morning, Shuri.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.410
Shuu-chan, Shuri-chan, morning.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.620
Morning.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.350
Morning, Aoi-san.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.790
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.060
<i>Now that I think about it, she's a year older than us.</i>

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.480
<i>I wonder if it's strange to call her 'chan'.</i>

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.280
<i>Maybe I should start calling her 'san' instead.</i>

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.600
Nanaka-chan!

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.490
Morning.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.520
So you're all 2nd year students starting this spring.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.080
Next year, you'll be taking your exams. Then soon after...

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.470
...your ability to read and understand Japanese...

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.980
The Important Melody

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.460
<i>I know yesterday was definitely my fault...</i>

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:59.150
<i>...but you don't have to have that kind of attitude.</i>

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.310
It's totally packed.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:19.980
Dammit, we're too late.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.030
In that case, we've gotta use <i>that</i>, right?

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.710
That's right.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.260
What's 'that'?

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.680
Here we go, Shuusuke!

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.990
Face that mountain and...

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.660
...jump!!

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.620
Don't tell me!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.390
I'm not gonna do something so silly.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.620
Attack!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.170
Wait.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:58.230
Cutlet sandwich, croquette bun, curry bun and a choco cornet.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.500
Curry bun, egg sandwich and a melon bun.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.640
Crab bun, crab bun and a choco cornet.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.370
That's a pretty harsh line-up for lunch.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.010
What can I do?

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:18.380
When I reached the bread stand, this was all that was left.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:23.760
I love crab buns and choco cornets. Do you dislike them, Sana-chan?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.760
Well, I don't dislike them either, but this is a bit lacking for lunch.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.420
By the way, why are you wearing an apron?

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:40.940
Ah, you see, I spill my food whenever I eat. 
This is so my uniform doesn't get all dirty.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.530
I see. That's why you wore an apron yesterday too.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:49.160
I'm smart, aren't I?

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.480
Yes, very...

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:58.820
We have to decide on the class representatives today.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.610
Do we have any volunteers?

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.970
No one?

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.470
This is a problem.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.940
In that case...

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:14.730
...it'd be easier to pick someone with experience.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:16.110
Yatsushiro-san?

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:17.400
Yes?

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:21.540
You were the class rep last year, weren't you?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:22.840
I was.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.890
I'm sorry, but would you mind taking that responsibility again this year?

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.220
I don't mind.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.640
That helps a lot.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.480
In that case, I should get an experienced person for the boys too.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.140
The lucky half of the Wakatsuki twins!

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.550
That's not a very nice way to address me!

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:47.130
You too, were a class rep last year, weren't you?

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:52.290
That was because the class nominated me while I was absent with the flu.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.360
That's right!

00:05:54.360 --> 00:06:02.430
Sensei, I, Wakatsuki Shuusuke, nominate Hidaka Sana-kun as 2-F's class rep.

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:05.960
What are you saying Shuu?

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:09.460
I just transferred! I can't be something like the class rep!

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.790
Don't be so modest.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:16.230
Weren't you always the leader when we used to play together.

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:19.760
If you utilise that leadership ability, then being a class rep shouldn't be a problem.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.520
That was when we were kids, right?

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.450
Sensei, I'd like to nominate Hidaka-kun as well.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.820
Even you too, Shuri.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:32.570
The unlucky half is nominating you as well.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:36.980
Sensei, please don't address me like that either.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.860
<i>If he does the committee work, then he might be able to fit into the class quicker.</i>

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.230
Alright. Those who agree, please raise your hands.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.040
Yes.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.930
Hey, wait up.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.010
What is it?

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.470
We're going to have a committee meeting after this, right?

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:11.470
But, I don't know where the audio visual room is, so I was wondering if we could go together...

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.250
Since you followed me here, just follow me as you please later.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.000
As I please?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:28.680
- Library -

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.530
<i>Isn't this the library?</i>

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.900
Ah, Sana-chan.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.300
Aoi-cha... No, I mean...

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.370
Aoi-san.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:51.920
Well, you know, you're a year older, and in the 3rd year.

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.590
So, I thought that it wouldn't be right to address you as 'chan'.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.480
Why? Just call me Aoi-chan like you always have.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:04.040
Should I? In that case...

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.360
By the way, Aoi-chan, why are you here?

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.320
Because I'm a librarian.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.440
- Library -

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.550
What about you? Did you come together with Nanaka-chan?

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:20.330
Well, actually...

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:24.010
So, that's what happened.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:27.340
Then, just read some books while you wait.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:34.570
Nanaka-chan always kills time here while waiting for the committee meeting to start.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.100
She always did that last year too.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.830
Last year?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.980
So that means, this would be your 2nd year being a librarian?

00:08:44.230 --> 00:08:45.870
No.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.690
This would be my 3rd year running!

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:58.460
Huh, you're still here?

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:01.220
I think Nanaka-chan already left.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.450
What's with Nanaka?

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:15.110
She knew that I didn't know where the audio visual room is, and yet...

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:16.750
Excuse me?

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.200
Are you going to the committee meeting as well?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:21.540
Yeah, I am.

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:26.370
Forgive me. I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:28.690
I overheard while passing by.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:35.250
I'm Hoshino Asami from class 2-E.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.370
I'm also a class rep. If you'd like, we can go to the audio visual room together.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:46.080
You're a transfer student?

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.210
Sorry, since you said you didn't know where the audio visual room was...

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:52.630
...I thought for sure that you were a freshman.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.600
From now on, if there's anything you're unsure about, feel free to ask.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.550
Thanks.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:00.550
- Audio Visual Room -

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:26.090
Hey, you could have at least said something before you left!

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.340
I never promised to do something like that.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:34.340
Besides, even though you didn't come with me, you managed to get someone to guide you here.

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.310
That's true, but...

00:10:37.310 --> 00:10:41.880
Okay now, since it's time, let's get started.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:44.310
First, we're going to rearrange the seating.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.310
In the first two rows, can we have the 1st year reps?

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:49.470
And in the next two rows, the 2nd year reps.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:52.140
And the 3rd year reps at the back.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:04.130
<i>What's with Nanaka?</i>

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:07.710
<i>She disappeared straight after the committee meeting.</i>

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.470
<i>Why is she acting that way?</i>

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.330
Hello?

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.780
Ah, mum.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.870
I'm fine.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.500
School?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:30.100
Yeah, I went.

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:32.420
You don't have to worry.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:35.700
No matter what, it'll go well.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.330
I'm so hungry.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.210
We've gotta fight our way through that crowd again?

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.020
What's with that glum look?

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.480
You're gonna get nothing but crab buns today again like that.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.600
Sana-chan!

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.560
Thank goodness! I made it in time.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.530
Here you go.

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:20.850
This is your bento.

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:22.070
For me?

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:25.890
Yep. I figured it was tough on you living alone.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.660
You really didn't have to.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:32.840
There's really not much difference between cooking for one and two people.

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:35.710
I'll make lunch for you every day!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.440
This is quite...

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.540
I can tell it was made with a lot of love.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:46.680
Isn't it cute that both of ours are the same?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.860
Yeah, it sure is cute, isn't it?

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:57.590
So, you two didn't go back together after the committee meeting?

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:58.840
Yeah.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.010
I see.

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:07.030
I thought that you could break the ice if you went to committee meetings together with Nanaka.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:11.450
So, is that why you nominated me?

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:13.420
Obviously.

00:13:13.420 --> 00:13:18.080
Unlike someone who sacrifices his friends to save himself.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.760
What are you saying? Of course I was planning that too.

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:29.940
What's with those eyes? 
Are you doubting my friendship?

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:37.870
But, why has Nanaka changed so much?

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:45.610
You know, it's because <i>that</i> happened yesterday and all.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:49.210
That's right. It was your fault there.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:54.210
Nice to meet you.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.940
Well, certainly, back then...

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.520
I didn't pinch it...

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.730
Yatsushiro-san?

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:38.890
I'd like to give this to Hidaka-kun.
 Can I leave it with you?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:41.540
Okay.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.110
Thank you.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:46.550
I'll leave it to you then.

00:14:48.810 --> 00:14:50.150
Hidaka-kun!

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.290
Hoshino-san.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.980
So you went through all that trouble to pass it to me?

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.400
I left the printouts with Yatsushiro-san.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.040
That.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.170
Thanks.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.100
Well, this is...

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:26.670
I ended up going home with Hoshino-san after the commitee meeting yesterday.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:31.590
And when I said I wanted to learn more about committee work back then...

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:35.770
...so these previous year's print outs...
-You're getting along pretty well with Hoshino-san.

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:39.270
It's not like we're getting along <i>that</i> well.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:43.490
Well, it's not something that involves me.

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:49.530
Even though today is our first lesson together, I'll be skipping the introductions.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.150
Instead, I'd like you all to hear my favourite song.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:58.410
Also, I'll be handing out questionnaires, so please write down your impressions of the song.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:04.060
Don't think too hard. Just freely write down whatever comes to mind.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.640
<i>The violin, huh?</i>

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:48.440
That's odd. Where's my pencil case?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.920
Maybe I left it in the music room during sixth period?

00:16:57.060 --> 00:16:58.750
Yatsushiro-san?

00:16:58.750 --> 00:16:59.680
Yes?

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:05.910
Sorry to trouble you, but, during the class earlier, I forgot and left...

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:08.360
...the impression questionnaires in the music prep room.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:13.360
It's probably inside the desk, so could you please get it for me?

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:15.090
Okay.

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:16.990
I'm counting on you then.

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.710
There it is!

00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:30.660
So, I did leave it here.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:48.770
It's not here.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:55.240
It wasn't in the desk now, was it?

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.130
Hoshino-san?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.830
I was passing by and I heard the piano playing.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:14.200
So, you know how to play the piano?

00:19:14.200 --> 00:19:16.620
I learned when I was a kid.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.070
Just a little.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:24.080
What's the name of that song? It was a very beautiful melody.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.450
It still doesn't have a name.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:30.720
I lived in this town my whole life.

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:34.000
Until five years ago, when we had to move because of circumstances at home.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:39.930
At my farewell party, my friend made this song as a present.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:44.430
It was only half-finished during the farewell party.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:50.390
In spite of that, it's a very important song to me.

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.320
It's strange, isn't it?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.550
Despite the fact that I've only heard it once.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:20:01.470
Quite some time has passed since I stopped playing the piano and I can no longer play any other songs.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:07.330
It was only half-finished, but for some reason, my fingers still remember the song, and only this one.

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:43.600
Yo.

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:47.440
Shuu, could you hold back a bit?

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.540
Sana, morning!

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:53.690
Even you too, Shuri.

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:55.420
Morning.

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:56.580
Ah, mornin...

00:21:25.990 --> 00:21:27.930
Finally, during episode 3...

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.520
...will the path at the crossroads end or will it continue?

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:34.400
The black & white of service, the next episode will be swimsuits!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.040
The promised follow-up will be there too.

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.510
There won't be.

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:39.880
Oh, really. Sorry.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.800
Next time on Myself; Yourself:
Cookies and Pebbles.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.220
The theme will be a love comedy.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:50.010
During the bath scene, you can get rid of the steam in the way if you put life into the controller.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:25:10.190
Cookies and Pebbles.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.910
It won't!

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:54.370
And what controller?
